      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I like PS2 them most\n\nInstead of introducting a new flag, you can use get_last_state_tc(port) \u003d\u003d tc_drp_auto_toggle\n\nso,\n\nif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_PD_DUAL_ROLE_AUTO_TOGGLE) \u0026\u0026 drp_state[port] \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON \u0026\u0026 get_last_state_tc(port) !\u003d tc_drp_auto_toggle) {\n  // We missed going through auto toggle state, reset back to unattached to ensure proper cycling\n  set_state_tc(port, power_role? SNK : SRC);\n}\n\nThis definitely seems like a hack but it is very limited; we should definitely figure out and fix long term why the state machine transitioning to low power mode instead of auto toggle\n\n\n---\n\nactually if I look at the state transitions into low_power_mode (https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c?q\u003df:platform/ec+port,%5C+tc_low_power_mode\u0026sq\u003dpackage:(%5Echromeos_internal$%7C%5Echromeos_public$)\u0026l\u003d2433\u0026dr\u003dC) the non auto toggle paths are guarded by conditions that say it is not AUTO_TOGGLE_ON. There is definitely something racy happening here",
